            <ArticleTitle>[Bilateral anterior uveiopapillitis, suspicious of Lyme disease--case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>23-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a patient which associated bilateral anterior uveitis manifestations with those of bilateral anterior inflammatory optic neuropathy. We followed the evolution of the case under treatment and we discussed the differential diagnosis and the association of the two ocular pathologies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
